# The built dashboard is deployed byte for byte, and the deploy workflow compares a hash
# of the served page against this file. Its line endings therefore must not depend on the
# operating system that checked it out: a Windows clone produced CRLF, git stored LF, and
# a deploy run from that clone shipped a page whose hash could never match the commit it
# came from. The content was identical and the check still failed, which is the worst kind
# of red -- correct code, failing gate.
dashboard/index.html   text eol=lf
dashboard/index.template.html text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: this one is read and executed by the page-behaviour tests.
tests/js/*.js text eol=lf
